{"ok":true,"result":{"id":"request-4","jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"content":[{"text":"<instruction>\n# Intent decisions\n\nExtract project -> business/brand/product -> outcome -> surface -> work item from current evidence. Preserve every requested goal, order and negative constraint. Read the original autonomy and decision-quality contracts before nontrivial outcome selection; context-quality applies when sufficiency, freshness, conflict or loss can change a decision.\n\nBefore choosing the next step, ask explicitly whether explanation only. If that condition is true, ANSWER directly as direct_explanation. Reading a helpful definition does not activate an action owner. Discussion about a fix, criticism, hypothetical work and quoted invocations remain explanation when the operator excludes action. Do not launch audit, repair, lifecycle, catalog or generic questionnaire merely because they are mentioned.\nBefore choosing the next step, ask explicitly whether actual explicit invocation. If that condition is true, Verify the original invocation-preflight grammar/checker before activation; first-token aliases use the original alias table. Invalid or ambiguous invocations activate no substitute. Preserve a valid named owner and its smallest safe mode.\nBefore choosing the next step, ask explicitly whether actual action requested AND few coherent enumerable targets/actions AND no material direction to choose AND focused proof sufficient. If that condition is true, SELECT direct_execution before a generic domain/lifecycle route, unless an explicitly named owner applies. This does not create a chantier or expand authority.\nELSE SELECT one outcome owner through surface. Load an unresolved routing matrix only if the owner remains unknown.\n\nClassify each material predicate TRUE, FALSE or UNKNOWN from evidence. UNKNOWN is never FALSE. Resolve discoverable facts with bounded evidence; make safe technical choices; ask only for operator-owned truth that changes the outcome, route, safety or effects. Use the original question contract before a routing question. State objective, owner/direct route, constraints, applicable protections, next action and re-entry condition before a dependent action.\n\n</instruction>","type":"text"}],"isError":false}}}
